    affiliation: "Universite Cote d'Azur"
repository-code: "https://github.com/romain-girardi-eng/EleutherIA"
url: "https://eleutheria.dev"
abstract: >-
  EleutherIA is an AI-powered scholarly research platform combining a
  FAIR-compliant knowledge graph, an ancient texts corpus, and an agentic
  GraphRAG engine to document ancient philosophical debates on free will,
  fate, and moral responsibility from the Greco-Roman and Early Christian
  periods (6th c. BCE - 6th c. CE). It features 17,700+ KG nodes, 42,900+
  edges, 189 ancient Greek/Latin works with 17,000+ passages, agentic
  multi-LLM reasoning, hybrid search, and citation-verified scholarly Q&A.
keywords:
  - ancient philosophy
  - free will
  - knowledge graph
  - GraphRAG
